CAVEAT:  This case measured the IPv6 NTP server role only. It did not test NTP
         authentication keys, `ntp peer`, `ntp pool` or an upstream server, so the DUT was
         always its own time reference (refid 127.127.1.1). One IPv6 client host was used,
         so this run does not show how the server behaves under many clients at once. The
         IPv6 leg was a single /64 with no router between the two ends, so this run does
         not cover a routed or multi-hop IPv6 path.
