STEP 4 -- `ntp restrict default-v6` refuses IPv6 clients and keeps serving IPv4    PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: this is the control that must NOT match. It runs against a live server, so the
  only thing that differs between the two legs is the address family.

awplus(config)#ntp restrict default-v6 serve deny
awplus#show running-config | include ntp
ntp master 7
ntp restrict default-v6 serve deny

    leg       client                              result
    ---       ------                              ------
    denied    fd32:b1f0:dff8:1603::1 (IPv6)       sent=3 replies=0 origin_echo=0
                                                  no_reply=3, ntpc exit 2
    allowed   10.38.22.33 (IPv4), same server,    sent=2 replies=2 origin_echo=2
              seconds later                       no_reply=0, stratum 7

  Removed again, and IPv6 service returned on the same leg:
awplus(config)#no ntp restrict default-v6
awplus#show running-config | include ntp
ntp master 7
  -> ntpc -6 ...: SUMMARY sent=2 replies=2 origin_echo=2, stratum 7
  => STEP 4 PASS: one command switched off time service for EVERY IPv6 client and left
     IPv4 untouched, measured on both legs within seconds of each other against one live
     server. The denial is silent: no kiss-o'-death packet and no ICMPv6. Note the
     removal form, because it is not symmetric: the stored line reads
     `ntp restrict default-v6 serve deny`, but it is removed with
     `no ntp restrict default-v6`. The `serve deny` part cannot be typed back. Copying a
     running-config line and putting `no ` in front of it does not work here.

